Comment: The Copyright line is taken from the NOTICE file at the root of this
 source tree, which is the project's own statement of who holds it ("Copyright
 (C) 2026 TheFirstIstari and contributors"). It is NOT taken from the LICENSE
 file: LICENSE is the AGPL v3 licence text verbatim and its header is FSF
 boilerplate, so a copyright holder read out of it would be invented. The
 identifier is the SPDX "or later" form because NOTICE grants "either version
 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version", and the same
 identifier is what packaging/arch/PKGBUILD and packaging/homebrew/irc-serve.rb
 carry. scripts/check-packaging.py asserts that all four agree with LICENSE, so
 this file cannot drift away from the other two without the gate going red.